This is the CTA or ending of your video. Traditional CTAs are so yesterday. Sure, they can work but are they actually inspiring the user to do something they weren't already planning to do? If you struggle with getting conversions despite strong 100% view-through rates, then you need to test new actions att the ends of your content. Up to you how you factor this into length testing, and whether you count the action as part of the video length, or you apply them as addendums. You already know what I'd suggest, which is to be intentional and test comprehensively. Yada yada. 

Okay, here are some action break downs that are reverse engineered from THE REAL THING. Choose wisely, but most importantly, have fun!

* **Solidify The Solution:** Don't sugarcoat it....just end by saying how everything you've stated in the video actually resolves their problem/meets their need.
* **Prompt A Search:** Test out a discovery action, instead of prompting a purchase (i.e., *"Search [Brand/Term] to [verb] [outcome/what they get from researching]).
* **Re-Frame Value:** Remind them of the opportunity costs they may have to pay by NOT doing what you have suggested. Then pitch the action :) 
